  "question": {
    "html": "<section class=\"context\"><p>The diagram represents an ideal, monatomic gas that first undergoes a compression, then an increase in pressure.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>An adiabatic process then increases the volume of the gas to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"5.0\\times 10^{-2 }m^{3}\"></span>.</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"a(i)\"><p><strong>a(i)</strong> Calculate the work done during the compression. [1]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"a(ii)\"><p><strong>a(ii)</strong> Calculate the work done during the increase in pressure. [1]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"b(i)\"><p><strong>b(i)</strong> Calculate the pressure following this process. [2]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"b(ii)\"><p><strong>b(ii)</strong> Outline how an approximate adiabatic change can be achieved. [2]</p></section>"
